00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Data Incident Investigator assembles schema, lineage, and dashboard clues
into one auditable report.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:31.000
This public demo uses a synthetic, credential-free fixture.
The Removed schema column preset fills editable incident fields.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:43.000
We ask why revenue dropped, then provide the affected dataset and symptom.
No production data is modified.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Start once. The agent performs bounded retrieval, deterministic scoring,
and report composition.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:05.000
The activity trail shows observable operations, not hidden reasoning.
Fixture execution makes zero model calls.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:31.000
The strongest result is a plausible contributor, not a confirmed cause.
Gross revenue was removed from upstream raw dot orders.
Visible factors total eighty-one percent, high.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Every hypothesis resolves to report evidence.
The schema-change fact and lineage evidence remain separate.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Within the displayed fixture bounds, analytics dot daily revenue is supported at distance one,
and Revenue overview at distance two, with paths and provenance.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:31.000
These are human-review proposals. Every recommendation is Not Executed.
The app never changes production or writes back.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:42.000
The completed result downloads as deterministic, sanitized U T F eight Markdown.
No server-side report file is stored.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:50.100
This service is fixture-only. Local DataHub M C P is bounded;
live validation and judging access remain open.
